---
import Layout from "@/layouts/Layout.astro";
import { APP_DISCLAIMER, APP_NAME } from "@/lib/brand";
---

<Layout
  title="How to request your BeReal data export and open the ZIP"
  description="Request a downloadable copy of your BeReal data through its official privacy contact, then open the export ZIP in a free, local browser viewer."
>
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-10 sm:py-16">
    <nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="mb-8">
      <a href="/" class="link link-primary">{APP_NAME}</a>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-balance">
      How to request your BeReal data export
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed">
      To browse your BeReal archive, first ask BeReal for a downloadable copy of
      your personal data. This viewer opens the files you receive. It does not
      connect to your BeReal account or submit a request for you.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm">
      Official sources checked on <time datetime="2026-10-04"
        >4 October 2026</time
      >. {APP_DISCLAIMER}
    </p>

    <section class="mt-10 space-y-4" aria-labelledby="request-data">
      <h2 id="request-data" class="text-2xl font-semibold">
        1. Contact BeReal about your data
      </h2>
      <p>
        BeReal's <a class="link link-primary" href="https://bereal.com/privacy"
          >privacy policy</a
        >{" "}
        lists its Data Protection Team at <a
          class="link link-primary"
          href="mailto:dpo@bere.al">dpo@bere.al</a
        >{" "}
        for data rights requests. Ask for a copy of your account data in a downloadable,
        machine-readable format. BeReal may ask for information to confirm that the
        account belongs to you.
      </p>
      <p>
        The <a
          class="link link-primary"
          href="https://help.bereal.com/hc/en-us/requests/new"
          >official Help Center request form</a
        >{" "}
        is another support contact. Its available categories can change. Follow BeReal's
        current instructions; this guide does not assume a particular in-app menu
        or promise a delivery time.
      </p>
      <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold">Example request</h3>
      <blockquote class="rounded-lg bg-base-100 p-5 leading-relaxed">
        Hello BeReal Data Protection Team. I would like a downloadable,
        machine-readable copy of the personal data associated with my BeReal
        account, including available posts, memories and their media. Please
        tell me what you need to identify my account and how I can securely
        receive the export. Thank you.
      </blockquote>
      <p>
        Add account details only in your private request to BeReal. Do not post
        them in this viewer's issue tracker.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 space-y-4" aria-labelledby="keep-export">
      <h2 id="keep-export" class="text-2xl font-semibold">
        2. Download and keep the original export
      </h2>
      <p>
        When BeReal provides your files, download them to your device and keep
        an unchanged copy. This viewer supports a BeReal ZIP containing JSON
        records and media, with an optional <code>.json.gz</code> analytics file.
        A standalone JSON file is not enough to import an archive here.
      </p>
      <p>
        The ZIP limit is 500 MiB and the optional compressed analytics limit is
        100 MiB. Expanded data and entry counts also have limits, listed on the
        <a class="link link-primary" href="/">viewer page</a>. Export formats
        and included records can vary; compatibility with every BeReal export is
        not guaranteed.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 space-y-4" aria-labelledby="open-export">
      <h2 id="open-export" class="text-2xl font-semibold">
        3. Open the ZIP and save your photos
      </h2>
      <ol class="list-decimal space-y-3 pl-6">
        <li>
          Open the viewer and select the BeReal ZIP. Add the analytics file if
          you have it.
        </li>
        <li>
          Select <strong>Analyze selected files</strong> and review the import report.
        </li>
        <li>
          Browse the available posts, memories, friends and conversations.
        </li>
        <li>
          Select <strong>Download complete archive</strong> to save media, or download
          selected posts and memories.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        Separate camera downloads preserve the original image format. Merged
        photos are JPEGs. Metadata includes timestamps and locations when they
        are available. The viewer cannot restore records missing from the
        export.
      </p>
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/#open-archive">Open your BeReal ZIP</a>
      <p>
        Free, no account or tracking. The browser reads your files locally,
        without uploading them. Refreshing clears imported data from memory;
        saved downloads remain on your device.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 space-y-4" aria-labelledby="export-questions">
      <h2 id="export-questions" class="text-2xl font-semibold">
        If you do not have a ZIP yet
      </h2>
      <p>
        Try <strong>Explore demo data</strong> on the viewer page. It uses invented
        records and illustrated images to show the browsing and download flow without
        personal files. An empty section in your own archive can mean BeReal did not
        include those records; check the import report before assuming the data was
        lost.
      </p>
      <p>
        Only BeReal can handle the data request. Check its current privacy
        policy for the rights and procedures that apply to you.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
